# EXTERNAL PATCH — DO NOT apply inside this repo.
#
# Rationale: The offending rule "Never use cat/grep/find/sed/ls. Use bat/rg/fd/sd/eza
# instead. Install via brew if missing." is rendered into the user-global
# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md inside the <!-- gentle-ai:persona --> managed block. The TRUE source
# of truth is the external gentle-ai Homebrew binary (gentleman-programming/tap), which
# embeds and regenerates this block; any manual edit to CLAUDE.md is reverted on the next
# gentle-ai run. The durable fix MUST be filed upstream against gentleman-programming/tap.
# The unconditional mandate assumes fd/eza/bat/sd exist; on hosts lacking them, agents shell
# out to fd/eza, the call returns empty (often with the error swallowed by 2>/dev/null), and
# the empty stdout is misread as "0 skills" — the root cause of the incident.
#
# The diff below targets the rendered persona block as a reference for the upstream template
# change. The line numbers reflect this host's ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (do NOT edit that file
# here; apply the equivalent edit to the gentle-ai persona template instead).
#
# Honors all three fix principles: PORTABLE DISCOVERY (prefer + command -v guard + POSIX
# fallback), FAIL-LOUD (ban bare 2>/dev/null and || true on discovery), REGISTRY-AUTHORITATIVE
# (presence is decided by the registry, never by a scan; empty scan is INCONCLUSIVE).

--- a/.claude/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/.claude/CLAUDE.md
@@ -545,7 +545,15 @@
 ## Rules

 - Never add "Co-Authored-By" or AI attribution to commits. Use conventional commits only.
-- Never use cat/grep/find/sed/ls. Use bat/rg/fd/sd/eza instead. Install via brew if missing.
+- PREFER bat/rg/fd/sd/eza when available, but ALWAYS guard with `command -v <tool>` and fall
+  back to portable POSIX tools (find/ls/cat/grep/sed). Never assume fd/eza/bat/sd exist; the
+  standard tools are valid fallbacks, not banned. Install the preferred tools via brew when
+  convenient, but never depend on their presence.
+- NEVER append `2>/dev/null` or `|| true` to a discovery command. You must SEE
+  `command not found` and other errors. A swallowed error on a discovery command is a defect.
+- Skill/file presence is determined by the registry (engram or .atl/skill-registry.md), NOT
+  by a filesystem scan. An empty or failed scan is INCONCLUSIVE, never proof of "zero" or
+  "absent". NEVER conclude that skills are missing or virtual from a scan that returned
+  nothing — re-run with portable tools and report the tool/error first.
 - Response-length contract: default to short answers. Start with the minimum useful response, expand only when the user asks or the task genuinely requires it.
 - Ask at most one question at a time. After asking it, STOP and wait.
 - Do not present option menus, exhaustive lists, or multiple approaches unless there is a real fork with meaningful tradeoffs.
